-- title:
--   Place differences generate the glued degree-zero class group
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra satisfying [`AlgebraicCurve.HasPrincipalDivisors K F`](def/AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup.html#L217), i.e. every nonzero $f \in F$ admits a divisor $D$ (an element of $\mathrm{Place}(K,F) \to_0 \mathbb{Z}$, places being the valuation subrings of $F$ that contain $K$, are not all of $F$ and are principal) with $D(v) = \mathrm{ord}_v(f)$ for all $v$ and $\deg D = 0$. Let $S$ be a finite set of pairs of places whose second coordinates are pairwise distinct (`Set.InjOn Prod.snd`), assume each $K \to \kappa(v)$ is surjective, and assume constants can be interpolated: for every finite set $E$ of places and every $c : \mathrm{Place}(K,F) \to K^\times$ there is $g \in F$ lying in each $v \in E$ with residue the image of $c(v)$ in $\kappa(v)$. Let $T_0, T_1$ be finite sets of places. Then the additive subgroup of $\mathrm{GluedPic}^0 = \mathrm{admissible}(S)/\mathrm{gluedPrincipal}(S)$ generated by the classes `mk S x` of admissible triples $x = (\delta_P - \delta_Q, 0, 0)$ with $P, Q \notin T_0$, together with those of the form $x = (0, \delta_P - \delta_Q, 0)$ with $P, Q \notin T_1$, is all of $\mathrm{GluedPic}^0$; here admissibility means both divisor components have degree zero and the first (resp. second) vanishes at every first (resp. second) coordinate of a pair in $S$, and the third component lies in the group of functions $S \to \mathrm{Additive}(K^\times)$.
--
--   This is the generation statement for the generalized Jacobian of the curve obtained by gluing two copies of a curve along the pairs of points listed in $S$: a homomorphism out of $\mathrm{GluedPic}^0$ is determined by its values on the classes of single-copy place differences avoiding prescribed finite sets. It is used to compare endomorphisms (Hecke operators, degeneracy maps, Frobenius twists) of the special fibre of the Néron model of a modular curve with $\Gamma_0(p)$-structure.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_GluedPic0_closure_setOf_mk_single_sub_single_eq_top.lean

import Mathlib
